  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday) \nIssued at 1031 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nLate this week the anchored ridge across the Southeast will \ncontinue to retrograde and weaken as a cut off low moves westward \nacross Florida. What remains of the ridge will keep around warmer \nthan normal temps in place with highs in the mid to upper 90s and \nheat index values around 100 degrees Friday and Saturday.\n\nThis weekend, the low will continue to slide westward. However, \nmodels are now not as certain on what the path and trajectory of \nthe low will be as it is suggesting it slows down the westward \nprogression on Sunday and stalls it out to our south through \nMonday. This pattern leads to a greater assumption that the front \nwell to our north that drapes over into the OH Valley and Mid \nAtlantic will not make it through the TN Valley. The persistent \nsfc high along the east coast will cause it to become more of a \nwedge front for us on Sunday into Monday. Temps and POPs on Sunday\nand Monday will depend a lot on the pattern than ends up taking \nshape. However, there should be a downward temp trend with \nmodels favoring highs \"only\" in the 80s on Monday as medium rain \nchances (40-60%) move in.",
